\glspl{DenseNets} consist of multiple \text{\it dense} \text{\it blocks}, connected in series and separated by \textit{transition layers}.
Each transition layer consists of a $1 \times 1$ convolution layer and a $2 \times 2$ average pooling layer.
Fig.~\ref{fig:DenseNet3b} illustrates how these \text{\it dense blocks} and \text{\it transition layers} are composed in \glspl{DenseNets}. Note that pooling is only performed outside of \text{\it dense blocks}.

