\section{Conclusions}
This paper investigates noise robustness of \glspl{DenseNets} and their extension with domain adversarial learning. Our experimental results demonstrate that \glspl{DenseNets} are more robust against noise than other types of neural networks. Furthermore, we show that applying domain adversarial learning improves the performance of \glspl{DenseNets} and model generalization.
